From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JarvisNano <jarvisnano@local>
Date: Thu, 22 May 2026 11:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] waveform: round-display redesign — concentric rings fill 466x466

HARDWARE FEEDBACK: the waveform read as a thin horizontal sliver on the round
panel — wrong primitive. Redesign to fill the circular 466x466 display with
concentric rings + a rotating arc, centred on the panel.

CHANGES (all in waveform.c, same dsc/buffer/task plumbing as 0031+0033):
- Geometry: FACE_H 120 -> 466 (square buffer covering the round panel). Buffer
  466*466*2 colour + 466*466 alpha = 651,468 B/frame; x2 double-buffer = ~1.24 MB
  PSRAM. Verified headroom: board is 8 MB octal PSRAM (CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT),
  app ~2.5 MB, emote buffers small — 1.24 MB fits comfortably. malloc keeps the
  internal-RAM fallback.
- Renderers replaced (bars/line/scan -> rings):
    IDLE      one calm breathing ring (r~150-164), radius+brightness pulse.
    LISTENING/SPEAKING  5 concentric rings (r=70..220); inner always on, outer
                        light up + thicken with amplitude (+ shimmer) — the
                        recognisable round voice visualiser.
    THINKING  a bright ~63deg arc sweeps around a dim full ring (r=165).
  New draw_ring_arc(buf, r, half_thickness, colour, alpha, arc_from, arc_to)
  strokes a (partial) ring by walking angle so it stays smooth at large radii.
- px(), clear_frame, the dsc, the 20 fps eased task, and the amplitude source
  (synthetic + the 0032 audio bridge) are UNCHANGED.

SPIRAL CAN'T RECUR — verified the descriptor matches the buffer EXACTLY:
- gfx_image_dsc_t built as ONE designated-initializer literal (from 0033),
  header.w=FACE_W=466, header.h=FACE_H=466, stride/flags = 0 (reference style).
- gfx_img_set_src sets obj->geometry.w/h = header.w/h, and the blend derives
  src_stride = header.w = 466 (gfx_img.c:117) = the buffer's real row pitch
  (px() indexes y*FACE_W+x, FACE_W=466). No pitch mismatch ⇒ no row shear.
- data_size = w*h*2 + w*h = 651468 (same formula the reference uses).
- The 0033 colour byte-swap (__builtin_bswap16 RGB565 macro) is retained.

Carried by apply_reactive_waveform_face_patch, which (since 0033) ALWAYS
re-copies the vendored firmware/emote/waveform.c — so this redesign installs on
both clean and incremental trees with no new bootstrap step.

Bundle order for the combined build: 0030 (6MB partition) + 0031 (waveform) +
0033 (colour+dsc) + 0034 (round) + 0032 (audio bridge) + voice-eng's Gemini fix.
Syntax-checked the ring renderers under -Wall (no warnings). Did NOT flash/build.
---
diff --git a/components/common/emote/waveform.c b/components/common/emote/waveform.c
--- a/components/common/emote/waveform.c
+++ b/components/common/emote/waveform.c
@@ geometry @@
-#define FACE_H            120
-#define FACE_BARS         48
+#define FACE_H            466
+#define FACE_RINGS        5
+#define FACE_R_MAX        220
+#define FACE_R_MIN        70
@@ renderers @@
- draw_bar / render_idle(line) / render_bars(vertical bars) / render_thinking(gaussian sweep)
+ draw_ring_arc / render_idle(breathing ring) / render_bars(concentric amplitude rings) / render_thinking(rotating rim arc)
